        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Penal Code, 1860",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 560,
          "end": 583
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2685074806213379
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "The gist of the prosecution as evident from the FIR relates to three loans having been borrowed by the appellant by mortgaging two properties and out of which one 1 Crl.No.___ of 2025 @ SLP (Crl.) No.15176/2025 19:04:18 IST",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 585,
      "end": 808,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Crl.No.___ of 2025",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 750,
          "end": 768
        },
        {
          "text": "SLP (Crl.) No.15176/2025",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 771,
          "end": 795
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2523493468761444
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "Reason:\nproperty has been sold by suppressing the factum of same having been mortgaged,\nthat too by manipulating with the revenue records.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 809,
      "end": 947,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2501966655254364
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "This fact of the second property having been mortgaged is seriously disputed by the appellant.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 948,
      "end": 1042,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2661774754524231
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Anyway, it would be in the discretion of the trial court to thrash same after full-fledged trial.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1043,
      "end": 1140,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2887248396873474
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "If we embark upon any inquiry in this regard, it would naturally prejudice the rights either of the parties.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1141,
      "end": 1249,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.22657062113285065
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "Hence, we desist from undertaking such an exercise.\n4.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1250,
      "end": 1304,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.19954320788383484
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "The issues raised in the compliant by respondent No.2 and rebutted by the appellant  accused as noticed hereinabove would be subject matter of trial and as such custodial interrogation of appellant would not be warranted.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1305,
      "end": 1526,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3329208195209503
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "Harbhag Singh vs The State Of Haryana on 5 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/4006879/\n1",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1527,
      "end": 1640,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Harbhag Singh vs The State Of Haryana on 5 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1528,
          "end": 1599
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "The allegations made in the complaint relates to the documentary evidence and that too registered documents.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1641,
      "end": 1749,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3114290237426758
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 17,
      "text": "Hence, we are of the considered view that appellant is entitled for being released on anticipatory bail.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1750,
      "end": 1854,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.30001190304756165
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "Hence, we direct the 2 Crl.No.___ of 2025 @ SLP (Crl.) No.15176/2025 Investigating Officer to release the appellant on anticipatory bail on such terms and conditions including the condition of directing him to appear before the Investigating Officer as and when called upon.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1855,
      "end": 2129,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Crl.No.___ of 2025",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1878,
          "end": 1896
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.176091268658638
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "With these observations, the appeal stands disposed of.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 2130,
      "end": 2185,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.05969765782356262
    },
